            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I spent some time tracing this to understand where the behavior comes from, and I wanted to share what I found before continuing down one implementation path.\n\nFrom what I found, the custom `tabline` path in `win_redr_stl_expr()` starts with `TabLineFill` as the base highlight (`attr = HL_ATTR(HLF_TPF)`), and later every explicit `%#...#` highlight is combined with that base using `hl_combine_attr(attr, curattr)`.\n\nI also experimented with making explicit `%#...#` groups bypass the base highlight for the custom tabline, now that makes the reported issue disappear but it also breaks the existing `tabline combines highlight attributes` functional test. So it seems that inheriting unspecified attributes from the base highlight is intentional behavior in general, not just for the tabline.\n\nI also tried a change that skips the combine only for `TabLine`/`TabLineSel`. That fixes the reported issue and passes the existing tabline tests but it also feels like a special case thing.\n\nBefore continuing with either approach, I wanted to understand the intended behavior.\n\nShould the custom `tabline` intentionally behave differently for `TabLine`/`TabLineSel` so that it matches the built-in `draw_tabline()` renderer, or is the preferred direction to keep the renderer as-is and instead make `TabLineSel` define a complete default highlight (for example by giving it an explicit background)?",
