            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> So it seems that inheriting unspecified attributes from the base highlight is intentional behavior in general, not just for the tabline\n\nyes, see aforementioned #29976, and also #31575 and #32060\n\n> feels like a special case thing\n\nyes, doesn't feel right\n\n> Should the custom tabline intentionally behave differently for TabLine/TabLineSel so that it matches the built-in draw_tabline() renderer\n\nbetter the other way around: the built-in C implementation should behave more like `win_redr_stl_expr`, so that over-all consistency is increased\n\n> make `TabLineSel` define a complete default highlight\n\nI agree with @ribru17, this sounds like the only sensible solution to me",
